<title>USA: Air Force to choose rocket finalists - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Air Force to choose rocket finalists - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A $1.4 billion contest is under ay among McDonnell Douglas, Lockheed Martin, Boeing and Alliant to develop a new line of all-purpose rockets for the Pentagon, The Wall Street Journal reported Friday.</p>
<p>The Air Force on Monday is expected to choose two finalists from among the four rivals, the story says.</p>
<p>The new family of rockets is intended to reduce government launch costs by 25 percent to 50 percent, the story says.</p>
